From b94de6497e5384c80d513352477b88ac7d365d25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Prateek Mittal <finance.prateek.mittal@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 06:07:19 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] a2dp: Recover from a failed reconfiguration

Close can only be sent from OPEN or STREAMING.  The error path then
aborted the stream unconditionally, including when a Close was already in
flight, and a failed SetConfiguration tore down the endpoint even though
the previous configuration was still valid.

- Reject a second request with EBUSY while a Close or Abort is pending,
  and do not Abort a stream that cannot be closed.
- Save the active capabilities and SEPs before closing, then restore them
  if the remote or the local endpoint rejects the new configuration.
- Propagate the A2DP configuration error name to the caller and return
  InvalidArguments for malformed vendor configurations, without touching
  the current stream.

Assisted-by: DeepSeekHarness:deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017
---
 profiles/audio/a2dp.c | 387 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 356 insertions(+), 31 deletions(-)

diff --git a/profiles/audio/a2dp.c b/profiles/audio/a2dp.c
index 37f6d4a..858023d 100644
--- a/profiles/audio/a2dp.c
